"relationship": "same_topic",
"comparison": "Both Bank of America and Citi disclose that legal and regulatory actions result in significant financial penalties and reputational harm that may exceed established reserves or have material negative effects. BAC specifically states that judgments and fines \"may be significant or unpredictable, and in some cases, exceed the amount of reserves established\" (bac_2024_1A_P103_S002), while Citi warns that it may be subject to \"substantial fines and penalties\" and requirements that could \"materially and negatively affect Citi's businesses... financial condition or results of operations\" (c_2024_1A_P136_S004). Both identify the unpredictability and severity of these remedies as key risks.",
