"relationship": "same_topic",
"comparison": "BAC and Citi both highlight the difficulty in predicting legal outcomes and the uncertainty inherent in estimating losses. BAC notes that legal risks involve \"unpredictable outcomes\" (bac_2024_1A_D040), whereas Citi explicitly states that for complex claims, \"The outcome of such proceedings is difficult to predict or estimate until late in the proceedings\" (c_2024_1A_P137_S002) and that accrual estimates involve \"significant judgment and may be subject to significant uncertainty\" (c_2024_1A_P137_S003). Both disclosures underscore that the unpredictability of regulatory and legal environments complicates financial planning and reserve adequacy.",
