"peer_ticker": "GS",
"peer_disclosure_id": "gs_2024_1A_D088",
"relationship": "same_topic",
"comparison": "Goldman Sachs and Bank of America both report high volumes of legal claims and the risk that actual outcomes may exceed reserves due to the uncertain regulatory environment. BAC states that fines and penalties may \"exceed the amount of reserves established\" (bac_2024_1A_P103_S002), while GS explains that the \"uncertain regulatory enforcement environment makes it difficult to estimate probable losses, which can lead to substantial disparities between legal reserves and subsequent actual settlements or penalties\" (gs_2024_1A_P136_S003). Both firms also acknowledge facing a \"high volume of claims\" (gs_2024_1A_P135_S001) and significant legal risks (bac_2024_1A_P099_S001).",
