"peer_disclosure_id": "gs_2024_1A_D086",
"relationship": "related_topic",
"comparison": "Both BAC and GS disclose risks related to increased regulatory scrutiny and the resulting costs or operational impacts. BAC warns that regulatory actions could \"impose additional compliance and other costs\" and \"require us to increase prices\" (bac_2024_1A_P097_S003), while GS highlights that \"Governmental scrutiny from regulators... remains at high levels\" and that penalties and fines sought by authorities \"have increased substantially\" (gs_2024_1A_P130_S001, gs_2024_1A_P131_S002). Both firms link regulatory enforcement actions directly to adverse financial and operational consequences.",
