"peer_ticker": "JPM",
"peer_disclosure_id": "jpm_2024_1A_D116",
"relationship": "same_topic",
"comparison": "Bank of America and JPMorgan Chase both explicitly state that legal and regulatory outcomes may exceed the reserves they have set aside. BAC discloses that penalties and fines may \"exceed the amount of reserves established\" (bac_2024_1A_P103_S002), and JPMorgan states that its exposure \"could, in some cases, exceed the amount of reserves that JPMorganChase has established for those matters\" (jpm_2024_1A_P217_S003). Both firms also identify that these regulatory actions can lead to restructuring or cessation of products/services (bac_2024_1A_P097_S003; jpm_2024_1A_P217_S001), impacting profitability and reputation.",
