{
"peer_ticker": "MS",
"peer_disclosure_id": "ms_2024_1A_D036",
"relationship": "same_topic",
"comparison": "Both Bank of America and Morgan Stanley disclose that legal and regulatory actions can result in adverse judgments, fines, and penalties that materially affect business operations and reputation. BAC notes that these actions result in \"judgments, orders, settlements, penalties and fines adverse to us\" which may \"exceed the amount of reserves established\" (bac_2024_1A_P103_S002). Similarly, Morgan Stanley states that investigations may result in \"adverse judgments, settlements, fines, penalties\" and that significant action could \"materially adversely affect our business, reputation, financial condition or results of operations\" (ms_2024_1A_P073_S004, ms_2024_1A_P074_S001). Both firms acknowledge the broad scope of potential adverse outcomes from the same regulatory trends.",
